# Build output
bin/
obj/
# Anchored to the root, where `dotnet pack -o artifacts` writes. Unanchored, the pattern matched
# any folder of that name at any depth — and case-insensitively on Windows — so the Accessibility
# feature's Artifacts/ source folder was never committed, and a fresh clone did not build.
/artifacts/
# build.bat's output, ~2 GB. Anchored like /artifacts/.
/dist/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# IDE
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# The agent's folder: the mutation harness and its sweep drivers, settings, notes, worktrees and
# per-run backups. Developer-local, none of it published.
/.claude/

# The sample corpus is deliberately not committed (CLAUDE.md, "Testing"): it is developer-local and
# resolved through TestCorpus / TETITULZ_PDF_CORPUS. Corpus-gated tests report Skipped without it.
tests/pdf/
# Anchored for the same reason as /artifacts/: unanchored, it also swallowed the Studio app's
# Resources/Raw folder.
/raw/
# The JPEG 2000 corpus (PLAN.md Wave 15): a sparse clone of github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg-data,
# resolved through TestCorpus.JpxRoot / TETITULZ_JPX_CORPUS. Not committed: that repository states
# no licence.
/tests/jpx/

# Licensed standards, ~92 MB. These are reference copies obtained under a single-user licence whose
# own pages read "Single user only, copying and networking prohibited", so they do not belong in a
# history that might be pushed. They stay on disk: nothing builds or tests against them, and the
# documentation guard checks paths that still resolve locally.
#
# Reverse this by deleting the line if the repository is and will remain private and you hold a
# licence that permits it — but note that removing them from history afterwards is far harder than
# adding them now.
docs/iso/

# A 236 MB source archive, not project source.
*.7z

# The API-surface guard writes "<baseline>.actual" beside a baseline only when the comparison FAILS
# (or the baseline is missing): it is what you copy over the baseline to accept an intended change,
# and it says nothing once a run is green. Three were committed from earlier red runs — a tracked
# one is a failing run's leftovers sitting next to the file it is mistakable for.
tests/ApiSnapshots/*.actual

# The developer's harnesses: fuzzing, the corpus scorecard and fetcher, the package-consumption
# check, the table generators, the BenchmarkDotNet project. Developer-local, not published.
/tools/
/benchmarks/

# Security reviews are working records: the open items are GAPS.md's, the policy SECURITY.md's.
/docs/security-review-*.md

# The developer's own scripts: the local build, clean and helper batch files, and C# script files.
*.bat
*.csx

# The developer's register of open work and the plans: not published.
/GAPS.md
/PLAN*.md

# The owner's real invoices (GAPS.md §4a). Private: never committed, never a fixture; tests reach
# them through TestCorpus like any other corpus.
/private_invoices/

# Oracle tests (outside tools as second opinions) stay local
/oracle-tests/

# Work logs and assistant notes stay local
/local-notes/
